      "message": "HttpServletRequest.getRemoteAddr() can return null (Jetty edge cases, request fakes).\n\nThe previous code NPE\u0027d in isIpv6Address() before reaching the trust check. Treat a null peer address as untrusted and emit a rate-limited warning? Also a test could be added for that.\n\n```suggestion\n    String remoteAddress \u003d proxyAddressProvider.getRemoteAddr(req);\n    if (remoteAddress \u003d\u003d null) {\n      logger.atWarning().atMostEvery(1, TimeUnit.MINUTES).log(\n          \"Null remote address - HTTP header authentication rejected\");\n      return false;\n    }\n```",
